---
/**
 * A book leaf for page turns (src/scripts/book/turn.ts).
 *
 * Two hinged segments: the inner 60% of the page rotates about the spine, and the outer 40% rotates
 * slightly further mid-turn and back, so the leaf bends like paper. Each segment has a front and
 * back face, each clipping its content with overflow rather than clip-path (which would be
 * re-clipped on every frame of a 3D turn). A highlight runs along the fold.
 *
 * Faces are empty until a turn: the script inserts copies of the page images and removes them
 * afterwards. Purely decorative; the leaves layer is hidden from assistive technology.
 */
---

<div class="leaf" data-leaf>
  <div class="leaf__inner" data-leaf-inner>
    <div class="leaf__face leaf__face--front" data-face="inner-front"></div>
    <div class="leaf__face leaf__face--back" data-face="inner-back"></div>
    <div class="leaf__outer" data-leaf-outer>
      <div class="leaf__face leaf__face--front" data-face="outer-front"></div>
      <div class="leaf__face leaf__face--back" data-face="outer-back"></div>
    </div>
    <span class="leaf__fold" data-leaf-fold></span>
  </div>
</div>
